---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Vareno GTA 6 Guide';
const description =
  'Vareno’s GTA 6 guide does not ask you to create an account. Portrait photos are sent to RunComfy to make the image and are not sold.';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} schemas={[breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)]}>
  <article class="shell prose">
    <Crumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Reading the guides does not require an account. The only personal file this site asks for is the photo you
      choose to upload on the portrait tool.
    </p>
    <h2>The portrait photo</h2>
    <p>
      When you create a portrait, the server sends that photo to RunComfy so Google’s Nano Banana 2 Edit model can
      make a new image. The photo is held in server memory only long enough to run that request, or for up to 15
      minutes if the image service has to fetch it from a short-lived link on this site. We do not sell the photo and
      we do not build a public gallery from it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The tool allows 5 portraits an hour from the same network address. That counter stays in memory on the server.
      Use a photo you have the right to upload.
    </p>
    <h2>Ads and store links</h2>
    <p>
      Store buttons go to PlayStation, Microsoft, or Rockstar and are marked as sponsored links. If an ad slot is
      turned on later, the ad partner’s own policy will apply to that slot. Empty slots are not filled with placeholder
      claims.
    </p>
    <p>This notice was last updated on November 16, 2026.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
